{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788291868938,"sessionID":"ses_fa17fa8b8ffeRDvLpqU7vbxt5Y","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_01a05e8064cb7cb0ae8f71c3","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"gh issue view 153"},"output":"title:\tRuling: delimit declarations explicitly\nstate:\tOPEN\nauthor:\tkantord (Dániel Kántor)\nlabels:\t\ncomments:\t0\nassignees:\t\nprojects:\t\nmilestone:\t\nissue-type:\t\nparent:\t\nsub-issues:\t\nsub-issues-completed:\t\nblocked-by:\t\nblocking:\t\nnumber:\t153\n--\nGrilled via docs/.grill/syntax-ergonomics.round.yaml, question record-argument-boundary (plans/language-oddities.md, issue #9's inventory).\n\n**Ruled: delimit declarations explicitly.** Replace the same-line heuristic (issues #10, #20) with a required terminator after every declaration -- the boundary becomes a token instead of a line-position fact.\n\n```toylang\nfn id(s: Str) -> Str = s;\n\n{a: 1}\n```\n\nImplementation: pick the terminator token (semicolon is the working example in the grill round; confirm during implementation it doesn't collide with anything else in the grammar), require it after every `fn` and `type` declaration, and retire the same-line same-line rule and its diagnostic once the terminator makes the ambiguity unreachable. Update the corpus-pinned test (record_body_after_definition) and docs/reference/syntax accordingly.\n","metadata":{"output":"title:\tRuling: delimit declarations explicitly\nstate:\tOPEN\nauthor:\tkantord (Dániel Kántor)\nlabels:\t\ncomments:\t0\nassignees:\t\nprojects:\t\nmilestone:\t\nissue-type:\t\nparent:\t\nsub-issues:\t\nsub-issues-completed:\t\nblocked-by:\t\nblocking:\t\nnumber:\t153\n--\nGrilled via docs/.grill/syntax-ergonomics.round.yaml, question record-argument-boundary (plans/language-oddities.md, issue #9's inventory).\n\n**Ruled: delimit declarations explicitly.** Replace the same-line heuristic (issues #10, #20) with a required terminator after every declaration -- the boundary becomes a token instead of a line-position fact.\n\n```toylang\nfn id(s: Str) -> Str = s;\n\n{a: 1}\n```\n\nImplementation: pick the terminator token (semicolon is the working example in the grill round; confirm during implementation it doesn't collide with anything else in the grammar), require it after every `fn` and `type` declaration, and retire the same-line same-line rule and its diagnostic once the terminator makes the ambiguity unreachable. Update the corpus-pinned test (record_body_after_definition) and docs/reference/syntax accordingly.\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"gh issue view 153","time":{"start":1788291868930,"end":1788291868934}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Let me start by reading AGENTS.md (already provided in the system prompt, but let me confirm) and the issue. Let me first look at the worktree.\n\nLet me start by reading the issue and understanding the repo structure.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05e80653f001iHdoy0aHzFANei","sessionID":"ses_fa17fa8b8ffeRDvLpqU7vbxt5Y","messageID":"msg_05e80582e001nw6fBp323PYEkG"}}
