{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788291948759,"sessionID":"ses_fa17fa8b8ffeRDvLpqU7vbxt5Y","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_01a05e819f647942980aa982","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"git show 630a6fa --stat"},"output":"commit 630a6faf4d534347556a08233960592faf2f54fc\nAuthor: Daniel Kantor <git@daniel-kantor.com>\nDate:   Fri Aug 28 17:46:21 2026 +0200\n\n    Bare application becomes the default call form\n    \n    Implements the revised f-x decision (draft.md, REVISED 2026-08-28) and its\n    scope addition from issue #19. The root-position confinement and the\n    definition-body suspension flag are gone; in their place, one rule at the\n    argument's start: an argument -- bare, parenthesized, braced, or a variant's\n    payload -- must start on the same line as its function. Calls move into the\n    atom layer, so a bare call composes as an operand (f x + y is f(x) + y) and\n    chains right-recursively through atom itself, and the ident-brace\n    record-argument sugar is now the same code path rather than separate\n    machinery: two call forms, bare default and parens disambiguator.\n    \n    Projection wins over bare application everywhere, so p.b in a record-literal\n    value position is the field access it looks like (issue #19, reproducer\n    pinned as the projection_in_record_value corpus case). The same reasoning\n    removes [ from the bare-argument starter set: indexing owns ident-[ in a\n    whitespace-insensitive token stream, so a Vec-literal argument keeps parens.\n    The same-line rule also closes the (-argument and record-argument reaches\n    across the definition boundary that the old flag never covered (issue #10,\n    pinned as record_body_after_definition); the postfix-[ reach remains open\n    and is re-scoped in the research-log entry.\n    \n    The two misleading diagnostics from the oddities inventory die: \"= extent v\"\n    now parses as the call it looks like, and a function name standing where a\n    value is needed reports \"is a function, not a value\" instead of \"is not\n    defined\". A cross-line bare argument is rejected with an error naming the\n    parens spelling, via the parser remembering where it declined a cross-line\n    argument and enriching the failure at exactly that token.\n    \n    Corpus, examples, and docs migrate to bare style where the argument is a\n    simple chain; every corpus output is unchanged, so the migration is\n    byte-neutral on all seven backends (the suite pins this). Calls whose\n    argument starts with [, ., or -, or is a compound expression, keep parens.\n    \n    Human-authored: the bare-default decision, the same-line rule, the sugar\n    unification, projection-over-application, and the migration mandate\n    (draft.md revision; issues #10, #19, #20)\n    Derived: the [ exclusion from bare-argument starters (forced by postfix\n    indexing, the decision's own reasoning for .); the migrated spellings\n    Agent-invented: the wording of the two new diagnostics, the\n    declined-cross-line mechanism behind the parens-spelling hint, and the\n    choice of which call sites read better bare\n    \n    Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GSzsg9yW5HvfsKQ9PE2FNV\n\n docs/guides/enums.md                               |   4 +-\n docs/guides/streams.md                             |   2 +-\n docs/reference/builtins/collect.md                 |   4 +-\n docs/reference/builtins/range.md                   |   2 +-\n docs/reference/syntax/functions.md                 |  12 +-\n docs/tutorial/02-records.md                        |   3 +-\n docs/tutorial/04-enums.md                          |   2 +-\n docs/tutorial/05-streams.md                        |   6 +-\n examples/adults.toy                                |   2 +-\n plans/language-oddities.md                         |   8 +\n ...sition-is-unsafe-at-any-undelimited-boundary.md |  13 +\n site/public/corpus.json                            | 103 +++++--\n src/check.rs                                       |   9 +\n src/parse.rs                                       | 298 ++++++++++-----------\n tests/bare_application.rs                          |  63 +++--\n tests/corpus/adults.yaml                           |   2 +-\n tests/corpus/enum_inputs.yaml                      |   2 +-\n tests/corpus/enum_inputs_reject.yaml               |   2 +-\n tests/corpus/enum_match_default.yaml               |   2 +-\n tests/corpus/enum_scalar_input.yaml                |   2 +-\n tests/corpus/enum_scalar_input_reject.yaml         |   2 +-\n tests/corpus/enum_vec_payload.yaml                 |   2 +-\n tests/corpus/inputs_records.yaml                   |   2 +-\n tests/corpus/inputs_scalars.yaml                   |   4 +-\n tests/corpus/jq_tutorial.yaml                      |   2 +-\n tests/corpus/jq_tutorial_step4.yaml                |   2 +-\n tests/corpus/jsonlines_enum_stream.yaml            |   2 +-\n tests/corpus/jsonlines_of_inputs.yaml              |   4 +-\n tests/corpus/jsonlines_of_lines.yaml               |   2 +-\n tests/corpus/lines_cat.yaml                        |   2 +-\n tests/corpus/lines_preserve_crlf.yaml              |   2 +-\n tests/corpus/lines_stream_signature.yaml           |   2 +-\n tests/corpus/lines_unterminated_final_line.yaml    |   2 +-\n tests/corpus/map_records.yaml                      |   2 +-\n tests/corpus/projection_in_record_value.yaml       |  11 +\n tests/corpus/range_basic.yaml                      |   2 +-\n tests/corpus/range_empty.yaml                      |   2 +-\n tests/corpus/record_body_after_definition.yaml     |  12 +\n tests/corpus/record_in_a_record.yaml               |   2 +-\n tests/corpus/record_in_a_record_two_deep.yaml      |   2 +-\n tests/corpus/type_alias.yaml                       |   2 +-\n tests/corpus/undeclared_input_fields.yaml          |   2 +-\n ...kend_llvm__native_agrees_where_it_compiles.snap |   4 +-\n ...ackend_rust__rust_agrees_where_it_compiles.snap |   4 +-\n ...ent_is_rejected_naming_the_parens_spelling.snap |   5 +\n ...trailing_minus_is_subtraction_not_negation.snap |   2 +-\n .../bare_application__cannot_be_an_operand.snap    |   5 -\n ...ication__cannot_be_followed_by_an_operator.snap |   5 -\n ...ion__projection_wins_over_bare_application.snap |   5 +\n 49 files changed, 379 insertions(+), 259 deletions(-)\n","metadata":{"output":"commit 630a6faf4d534347556a08233960592faf2f54fc\nAuthor: Daniel Kantor <git@daniel-kantor.com>\nDate:   Fri Aug 28 17:46:21 2026 +0200\n\n    Bare application becomes the default call form\n    \n    Implements the revised f-x decision (draft.md, REVISED 2026-08-28) and its\n    scope addition from issue #19. The root-position confinement and the\n    definition-body suspension flag are gone; in their place, one rule at the\n    argument's start: an argument -- bare, parenthesized, braced, or a variant's\n    payload -- must start on the same line as its function. Calls move into the\n    atom layer, so a bare call composes as an operand (f x + y is f(x) + y) and\n    chains right-recursively through atom itself, and the ident-brace\n    record-argument sugar is now the same code path rather than separate\n    machinery: two call forms, bare default and parens disambiguator.\n    \n    Projection wins over bare application everywhere, so p.b in a record-literal\n    value position is the field access it looks like (issue #19, reproducer\n    pinned as the projection_in_record_value corpus case). The same reasoning\n    removes [ from the bare-argument starter set: indexing owns ident-[ in a\n    whitespace-insensitive token stream, so a Vec-literal argument keeps parens.\n    The same-line rule also closes the (-argument and record-argument reaches\n    across the definition boundary that the old flag never covered (issue #10,\n    pinned as record_body_after_definition); the postfix-[ reach remains open\n    and is re-scoped in the research-log entry.\n    \n    The two misleading diagnostics from the oddities inventory die: \"= extent v\"\n    now parses as the call it looks like, and a function name standing where a\n    value is needed reports \"is a function, not a value\" instead of \"is not\n    defined\". A cross-line bare argument is rejected with an error naming the\n    parens spelling, via the parser remembering where it declined a cross-line\n    argument and enriching the failure at exactly that token.\n    \n    Corpus, examples, and docs migrate to bare style where the argument is a\n    simple chain; every corpus output is unchanged, so the migration is\n    byte-neutral on all seven backends (the suite pins this). Calls whose\n    argument starts with [, ., or -, or is a compound expression, keep parens.\n    \n    Human-authored: the bare-default decision, the same-line rule, the sugar\n    unification, projection-over-application, and the migration mandate\n    (draft.md revision; issues #10, #19, #20)\n    Derived: the [ exclusion from bare-argument starters (forced by postfix\n    indexing, the decision's own reasoning for .); the migrated spellings\n    Agent-invented: the wording of the two new diagnostics, the\n    declined-cross-line mechanism behind the parens-spelling hint, and the\n    choice of which call sites read better bare\n    \n    Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GSzsg9yW5HvfsKQ9PE2FNV\n\n docs/guides/enums.md                               |   4 +-\n docs/guides/streams.md                             |   2 +-\n docs/reference/builtins/collect.md                 |   4 +-\n docs/reference/builtins/range.md                   |   2 +-\n docs/reference/syntax/functions.md                 |  12 +-\n docs/tutorial/02-records.md                        |   3 +-\n docs/tutorial/04-enums.md                          |   2 +-\n docs/tutorial/05-streams.md                        |   6 +-\n examples/adults.toy                                |   2 +-\n plans/language-oddities.md                         |   8 +\n ...sition-is-unsafe-at-any-undelimited-boundary.md |  13 +\n site/public/corpus.json                            | 103 +++++--\n src/check.rs                                       |   9 +\n src/parse.rs                                       | 298 ++++++++++-----------\n tests/bare_application.rs                          |  63 +++--\n tests/corpus/adults.yaml                           |   2 +-\n tests/corpus/enum_inputs.yaml                      |   2 +-\n tests/corpus/enum_inputs_reject.yaml               |   2 +-\n tests/corpus/enum_match_default.yaml               |   2 +-\n tests/corpus/enum_scalar_input.yaml                |   2 +-\n tests/corpus/enum_scalar_input_reject.yaml         |   2 +-\n tests/corpus/enum_vec_payload.yaml                 |   2 +-\n tests/corpus/inputs_records.yaml                   |   2 +-\n tests/corpus/inputs_scalars.yaml                   |   4 +-\n tests/corpus/jq_tutorial.yaml                      |   2 +-\n tests/corpus/jq_tutorial_step4.yaml                |   2 +-\n tests/corpus/jsonlines_enum_stream.yaml            |   2 +-\n tests/corpus/jsonlines_of_inputs.yaml              |   4 +-\n tests/corpus/jsonlines_of_lines.yaml               |   2 +-\n tests/corpus/lines_cat.yaml                        |   2 +-\n tests/corpus/lines_preserve_crlf.yaml              |   2 +-\n tests/corpus/lines_stream_signature.yaml           |   2 +-\n tests/corpus/lines_unterminated_final_line.yaml    |   2 +-\n tests/corpus/map_records.yaml                      |   2 +-\n tests/corpus/projection_in_record_value.yaml       |  11 +\n tests/corpus/range_basic.yaml                      |   2 +-\n tests/corpus/range_empty.yaml                      |   2 +-\n tests/corpus/record_body_after_definition.yaml     |  12 +\n tests/corpus/record_in_a_record.yaml               |   2 +-\n tests/corpus/record_in_a_record_two_deep.yaml      |   2 +-\n tests/corpus/type_alias.yaml                       |   2 +-\n tests/corpus/undeclared_input_fields.yaml          |   2 +-\n ...kend_llvm__native_agrees_where_it_compiles.snap |   4 +-\n ...ackend_rust__rust_agrees_where_it_compiles.snap |   4 +-\n ...ent_is_rejected_naming_the_parens_spelling.snap |   5 +\n ...trailing_minus_is_subtraction_not_negation.snap |   2 +-\n .../bare_application__cannot_be_an_operand.snap    |   5 -\n ...ication__cannot_be_followed_by_an_operator.snap |   5 -\n ...ion__projection_wins_over_bare_application.snap |   5 +\n 49 files changed, 379 insertions(+), 259 deletions(-)\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"git show 630a6fa --stat","time":{"start":1788291948750,"end":1788291948758}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Let me look at the commits that introduced the same-line rule (issues #10 and #20). Let me look at the commit \"630a6fa Bare application becomes the default call form\" and \"5928893 Fix vec literals being swallowed as indicesafter a definition\".","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05e819fd7001XMGQMXIihuDCKP","sessionID":"ses_fa17fa8b8ffeRDvLpqU7vbxt5Y","messageID":"msg_05e819a310016ZUkt9UfGgFtLj"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788291949231,"sessionID":"ses_fa17fa8b8ffeRDvLpqU7vbxt5Y","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_01a05e819feb789087a4a71a","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"git show 5928893 --stat"},"output":"commit 5928893019e29fc7368f34e92d7f24f532230f5d\nAuthor: Daniel Kantor <git@daniel-kantor.com>\nDate:   Sun Aug 30 22:44:55 2026 +0200\n\n    Fix vec literals being swallowed as indices after a definition\n    \n    A definition's trailing expression used to claim any '[' that followed it as an\n    index, so a vec literal sitting on the next line -- the program body -- parsed as\n    an index on the definition's body and failed with 'expected an expression'.\n    Indexing now owns '[' on the same line as its base only, the same line rule call\n    arguments follow, so a line break keeps a definition's body from swallowing the\n    program's body.\n    \n    Fixes #148.\n    \n    Written by DeepSeek V4 Flash via opencode.\n    \n    Co-Authored-By: DeepSeek V4 Flash via opencode\n\n site/public/corpus.json                            | 28 ++++++++++++++++++++++\n src/parse.rs                                       |  7 ++++++\n tests/corpus/vec_body_after_definition.yaml        | 12 ++++++++++\n ...kend_llvm__native_agrees_where_it_compiles.snap |  4 ++--\n ...ackend_rust__rust_agrees_where_it_compiles.snap |  4 ++--\n 5 files changed, 51 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)\n","metadata":{"output":"commit 5928893019e29fc7368f34e92d7f24f532230f5d\nAuthor: Daniel Kantor <git@daniel-kantor.com>\nDate:   Sun Aug 30 22:44:55 2026 +0200\n\n    Fix vec literals being swallowed as indices after a definition\n    \n    A definition's trailing expression used to claim any '[' that followed it as an\n    index, so a vec literal sitting on the next line -- the program body -- parsed as\n    an index on the definition's body and failed with 'expected an expression'.\n    Indexing now owns '[' on the same line as its base only, the same line rule call\n    arguments follow, so a line break keeps a definition's body from swallowing the\n    program's body.\n    \n    Fixes #148.\n    \n    Written by DeepSeek V4 Flash via opencode.\n    \n    Co-Authored-By: DeepSeek V4 Flash via opencode\n\n site/public/corpus.json                            | 28 ++++++++++++++++++++++\n src/parse.rs                                       |  7 ++++++\n tests/corpus/vec_body_after_definition.yaml        | 12 ++++++++++\n ...kend_llvm__native_agrees_where_it_compiles.snap |  4 ++--\n ...ackend_rust__rust_agrees_where_it_compiles.snap |  4 ++--\n 5 files changed, 51 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"git show 5928893 --stat","time":{"start":1788291949229,"end":1788291949230}},"id":"prt_05e81a0ba001mahvONkDHaop1l","sessionID":"ses_fa17fa8b8ffeRDvLpqU7vbxt5Y","messageID":"msg_05e819a310016ZUkt9UfGgFtLj"}}
