{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788291974242,"sessionID":"ses_fa17fa8b8ffeRDvLpqU7vbxt5Y","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_01a05e8200c9753395343823","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-153/tests/corpus/input_annotation.yaml"},"output":"<path>/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-153/tests/corpus/input_annotation.yaml</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # The `input <type>` annotation by itself: it declares what stdin holds before the body reads\n2: # it, and the body's `input` resolves against the declared type rather than borrowing one from\n3: # the function's signature. A use where nothing expects anything would refuse without one\n4: # (\"cannot tell what `input` contains\"); the declaration is that type (issue #150).\n5: program: |\n6:   fn f(p: {x: Int, y: Int}) -> Int = p.x * 2 + p.y * 3\n7: \n8:   input {x: Int, y: Int}\n9:   f(input)\n10: \n11: input: |\n12:   {\"x\": 3, \"y\": 4}\n13: \n14: output: |\n15:   18\n16: \n17: node_types: [application, arith.add, arith.mul, input, int, projection, var]\n\n(End of file - total 17 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# The `input <type>` annotation by itself: it declares what stdin holds before the body reads\n# it, and the body's `input` resolves against the declared type rather than borrowing one from\n# the function's signature. A use where nothing expects anything would refuse without one\n# (\"cannot tell what `input` contains\"); the declaration is that type (issue #150).\nprogram: |\n  fn f(p: {x: Int, y: Int}) -> Int = p.x * 2 + p.y * 3\n\n  input {x: Int, y: Int}\n  f(input)\n\ninput: |\n  {\"x\": 3, \"y\": 4}\n\noutput: |\n  18\n\nnode_types: [application, arith.add, arith.mul, input, int, projection, var]","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-153/tests/corpus/input_annotation.yaml","text":"# The `input <type>` annotation by itself: it declares what stdin holds before the body reads\n# it, and the body's `input` resolves against the declared type rather than borrowing one from\n# the function's signature. A use where nothing expects anything would refuse without one\n# (\"cannot tell what `input` contains\"); the declaration is that type (issue #150).\nprogram: |\n  fn f(p: {x: Int, y: Int}) -> Int = p.x * 2 + p.y * 3\n\n  input {x: Int, y: Int}\n  f(input)\n\ninput: |\n  {\"x\": 3, \"y\": 4}\n\noutput: |\n  18\n\nnode_types: [application, arith.add, arith.mul, input, int, projection, var]","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":17,"totalLines":17,"truncated":false}},"title":"tests/corpus/input_annotation.yaml","time":{"start":1788291974228,"end":1788291974239}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"The `input <type>` declaration was derived from the same-line rule. So it's part of the same-line heuristic. The brief says \"retiring the same-line heuristic (parser + checker + error message)\".\n\nHmm, but the `input <type>` disambiguation is a real problem if we retire same_line entirely. Let me think about what happens.\n\nActually, wait. Let me reconsider. The `input <type>` declaration is read in `parse` after the defs loop. The defs loop breaks at `input`. Then:\n\n```rust\nlet input = match p.peek()? {\n    (Tok::Input, input_span) => {\n        let (next, next_span) = p.peek2()?;\n        if (next == Tok::LBrace || matches!(next, Tok::Ident(_)))\n            && p.same_line(input_span.end, next_span.start)\n        {\n            p.advance()?;\n            Some(p.type_expr()?)\n        } else {\n            None\n        }\n    }\n    _ => None,\n};\n```\n\nIf we remove the same_line check, then `input` followed by `{` or `Ident` is always a declaration. But then a program body that starts with `input` as a value followed by a record literal on the next line would be misparsed.\n\nHmm, but wait — is that a real program? `input` as a value followed by `{a: 1}` on the next line. What would that mean? `input` is a value; `{a: 1}` is a record literal. Two expressions in a row is not valid toylang. So `input\\n{a: 1}` as a program body is already a parse error (\"expected end of program, found `{`\"). So treating it as `input {a: 1}` declaration would change the error from \"expected end of program\" to a type error or a successful parse.\n\nHmm, actually wait. Let me reconsider. Is `input {a: 1}` a valid declaration? `input <type>` where type is `{a: 1}` — a record type with field `a` of type... wait, `1` is not a type. So `input {a: 1}` would fail to parse as a type. So it'd be a parse error either way, just a different message.\n\nBut consider `input\\n{a: Int}`. As a program body: `input` value, then `{a: Int}` — `Int` is not an expression, so parse error. As a declaration: `input {a: Int}` — valid record type declaration. Hmm, so the line break matters here.\n\nActually, let me look at the corpus cases for input annotation to understand the intended usage.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05e820193001G172715IKvL05O","sessionID":"ses_fa17fa8b8ffeRDvLpqU7vbxt5Y","messageID":"msg_05e81e8f5001CG9S1yGf7h1v1O"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788291974871,"sessionID":"ses_fa17fa8b8ffeRDvLpqU7vbxt5Y","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_01a05e8203f4702097126424","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-153/tests/corpus/let_multi_input_annotation.yaml"},"output":"<path>/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-153/tests/corpus/let_multi_input_annotation.yaml</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # The multi-binding `let` block, end to end, with the input type declared up front by an\n2: # `input <type>` annotation instead of borrowed from the first use of `input` -- the shape\n3: # found failing as \"expected end of program, found {\" when the annotation followed the\n4: # function (issue #150). The annotation types the same stdin the body reads, so the run\n5: # validates the fixture against it just as it would against an inferred type.\n6: program: |\n7:   fn f(p: {x: Int, y: Int}) -> Int =\n8:       let a = p.x * 2\n9:       let b = p.y * 3\n10:       a + b\n11: \n12:   input {x: Int, y: Int}\n13:   f(input)\n14: \n15: input: |\n16:   {\"x\": 3, \"y\": 4}\n17: \n18: output: |\n19:   18\n20: \n21: node_types: [application, arith.add, arith.mul, input, int, local, pipe, projection, var]\n\n(End of file - total 21 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# The multi-binding `let` block, end to end, with the input type declared up front by an\n# `input <type>` annotation instead of borrowed from the first use of `input` -- the shape\n# found failing as \"expected end of program, found {\" when the annotation followed the\n# function (issue #150). The annotation types the same stdin the body reads, so the run\n# validates the fixture against it just as it would against an inferred type.\nprogram: |\n  fn f(p: {x: Int, y: Int}) -> Int =\n      let a = p.x * 2\n      let b = p.y * 3\n      a + b\n\n  input {x: Int, y: Int}\n  f(input)\n\ninput: |\n  {\"x\": 3, \"y\": 4}\n\noutput: |\n  18\n","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-153/tests/corpus/let_multi_input_annotation.yaml","text":"# The multi-binding `let` block, end to end, with the input type declared up front by an\n# `input <type>` annotation instead of borrowed from the first use of `input` -- the shape\n# found failing as \"expected end of program, found {\" when the annotation followed the\n# function (issue #150). The annotation types the same stdin the body reads, so the run\n# validates the fixture against it just as it would against an inferred type.\nprogram: |\n  fn f(p: {x: Int, y: Int}) -> Int =\n      let a = p.x * 2\n      let b = p.y * 3\n      a + b\n\n  input {x: Int, y: Int}\n  f(input)\n\ninput: |\n  {\"x\": 3, \"y\": 4}\n\noutput: |\n  18\n\nnode_types: [application, arith.add, arith.mul, input, int, local, pipe, projection, var]","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":21,"totalLines":21,"truncated":false}},"title":"tests/corpus/let_multi_input_annotation.yaml","time":{"start":1788291974859,"end":1788291974869}},"id":"prt_05e820467001Vg5squQSfoz7jw","sessionID":"ses_fa17fa8b8ffeRDvLpqU7vbxt5Y","messageID":"msg_05e81e8f5001CG9S1yGf7h1v1O"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788291975322,"sessionID":"ses_fa17fa8b8ffeRDvLpqU7vbxt5Y","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_01a05e8206697eb0b3b4efb3","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-153/tests/corpus/record_body_after_definition.yaml"},"output":"<path>/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-153/tests/corpus/record_body_after_definition.yaml</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # The record-literal program body used to be swallowed across the definition boundary as an\n2: # argument to the definition's trailing `s` (issue #10). An argument must start on the same\n3: # line as its function, and this `{` does not.\n4: program: |\n5:   fn id(s: Str) -> Str = s\n6: \n7:   {a: 1}\n8: \n9: output: |\n10:   {\"a\":1}\n11: \n12: node_types: [int, record-literal]\n\n(End of file - total 12 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# The record-literal program body used to be swallowed across the definition boundary as an\n# argument to the definition's trailing `s` (issue #10). An argument must start on the same\n# line as its function, and this `{` does not.\nprogram: |\n  fn id(s: Str) -> Str = s\n\n  {a: 1}\n\noutput: |\n  {\"a\":1}\n\nnode_types: [int, record-literal]","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-153/tests/corpus/record_body_after_definition.yaml","text":"# The record-literal program body used to be swallowed across the definition boundary as an\n# argument to the definition's trailing `s` (issue #10). An argument must start on the same\n# line as its function, and this `{` does not.\nprogram: |\n  fn id(s: Str) -> Str = s\n\n  {a: 1}\n\noutput: |\n  {\"a\":1}\n\nnode_types: [int, record-literal]","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":12,"totalLines":12,"truncated":false}},"title":"tests/corpus/record_body_after_definition.yaml","time":{"start":1788291975315,"end":1788291975319}},"id":"prt_05e8206dc001Zj0bEHXPAZbaXf","sessionID":"ses_fa17fa8b8ffeRDvLpqU7vbxt5Y","messageID":"msg_05e81e8f5001CG9S1yGf7h1v1O"}}
