e-line behavior, and the docs tests. Let me look at tests/docs.rs and the step tests that have snapshots about the same-line error message.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05e82de730012MXNeBSmHyfITH","sessionID":"ses_fa17fa8b8ffeRDvLpqU7vbxt5Y","messageID":"msg_05e82d7a3001yzmFnjyXscDeld"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788292030622,"sessionID":"ses_fa17fa8b8ffeRDvLpqU7vbxt5Y","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"grep","callID":"call_01a05e82def4771386526a39","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-153/tests","pattern":"same line|same-line|cross.line|cross_line"},"output":"Found 6 matches\n/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-153/tests/bare_application.rs:\n  Line 3: //! delimited -- must start on the same line as its function, which is what keeps a\n\n  Line 39: /// The definition-body suspension is gone: `= length v` is a call, and the same-line rule is\n\n  Line 49: /// the call across lines.\n\n  Line 51: fn a_cross_line_argument_is_rejected_naming_the_parens_spelling() {\n\n  Line 81: /// to anchor on. The same-line rule is what keeps a trailing bare identifier in a body from\n\n\n/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-153/tests/snapshots/bare_application__a_cross_line_argument_is_rejected_naming_the_parens_spelling.snap:\n  Line 5: expected end of program, found `1`; an argument must start on the same line as its function -- write `inc(...)` to call across lines (at byte 35)\n","metadata":{"matches":6,"truncated":false},"title":"same line|same-line|cross.line|cross_line","time":{"start":1788292030590,"end":1788292030619}},"id":"prt_05e82df660014bE1UJ8SCg82ls","sessionID":"ses_fa17fa8b8ffeRDvLpqU7vbxt5Y","messageID":"msg_05e82d7a3001yzmFnjyXscDeld"}}
