{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788292261555,"sessionID":"ses_fa17fa8b8ffeRDvLpqU7vbxt5Y","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"grep","callID":"call_01a05e8664e576f3b750f7fd","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-153","pattern":"same line|same-line|same_line","include":"*.rs"},"output":"Found 17 matches\n/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-153/tests/bare_application.rs:\n  Line 3: //! delimited -- must start on the same line as its function, which is what keeps a\n\n  Line 39: /// The definition-body suspension is gone: `= length v` is a call, and the same-line rule is\n\n  Line 81: /// to anchor on. The same-line rule is what keeps a trailing bare identifier in a body from\n\n\n/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-153/src/parse.rs:\n  Line 407:     // recognized by the same-line rule a call argument follows: only when the type opens on\n\n  Line 414:                 && p.same_line(input_span.end, next_span.start)\n\n  Line 476:     /// The full source, kept alongside the advancing `input` so the same-line rule can look at\n\n  Line 534:                     \"{msg}; an argument must start on the same line as its function -- \\\n\n  Line 542:     /// Whether nothing but spaces and tabs sits between two byte offsets. The same-line rule for\n\n  Line 543:     /// call arguments: an argument, bare or parenthesized, must start on the same line as its\n\n  Line 546:     fn same_line(&self, from: usize, to: usize) -> bool {\n\n  Line 550:     /// The same-line rule applied at one call site: true when the argument starting at\n\n  Line 555:         if self.same_line(callee_span.end, arg_span.start) {\n\n  Line 653:             if !self.same_line(binding_start, value.span().end) {\n\n  Line 1167:                     // Indexing owns `[` on the same line only, the same rule call arguments\n\n  Line 1170:                     if !self.same_line(e.span().end, bspan.start) {\n\n  Line 1259:     /// argument starts after it on the same line, or a plain variable reference.\n\n\n/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-153/src/check/mod.rs:\n  Line 1042:     // The same linearity a stream-typed parameter gets: `|` is the one construct that can\n","metadata":{"matches":17,"truncated":false},"title":"same line|same-line|same_line","time":{"start":1788292261532,"end":1788292261552}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"The \"is a function, not a value\" message is a different diagnostic (about `f -1` where `-` can't start a bare argument). That's not the same-line diagnostic. It should stay.\n\nSo the \"checker\" part of the brief's \"retiring the same-line heuristic (parser + checker + error message)\" — I think the \"checker\" here refers to the fact that the parse error message is what the checker surfaces, or it's just loosely worded. The actual same-line diagnostic is in parse.rs. Let me search the checker for any other same-line-related message.\n\nActually, let me search for \"same line\" in the whole repo (excluding plans and research-log).","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05e866571001bebAAyUb51YAPQ","sessionID":"ses_fa17fa8b8ffeRDvLpqU7vbxt5Y","messageID":"msg_05e865aec001yfwgrk5jH9NZ0N"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788292261854,"sessionID":"ses_fa17fa8b8ffeRDvLpqU7vbxt5Y","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"grep","callID":"call_01a05e8666377aa0b9a25ab0","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-153","pattern":"same line|same-line|same_line","include":"*.md"},"output":"Found 13 matches\n/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-153/docs/reference/syntax/functions.md:\n  Line 62: An argument must also start on the same line as its function; to call across lines, use the\n\n\n/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-153/research-log/juxtaposition-is-unsafe-at-any-undelimited-boundary.md:\n  Line 66: bare, parenthesized, braced, or a variant's payload -- must start on the same line as its\n\n\n/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-153/plans/module-routing-research.md:\n  Line 80: arms to files, but it is the precedent in the same lineage for \"a file of definitions named from\n\n\n/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-153/plans/language-oddities.md:\n  Line 127: form, confined only by the same-line rule, and both diagnostics above are gone -- `= extent v`\n\n  Line 152: Resolved by the same-line rule (issues #10 and #20): an argument, bare or delimited, must start\n\n  Line 153: on the same line as its function, so the swallowed program body above parses now; the corpus\n\n\n/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-153/plans/draft-split.md:\n  Line 114: same-line rule, the `-` and capitalized-callee exclusions), `reference/prelude/` or a small\n\n\n/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-153/CONTEXT.md:\n  Line 64: argument, or a call spread across lines, since an argument must start on the same line as its\n\n\n/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-153/draft.md:\n  Line 794: same line between `Iterator::sum` and `Iterator::fold`.\n\n  Line 945: with an associative one is. That is the same line the `reduce`/`fold` split already draws, now\n\n  Line 2023: the root-position confinement and the definition-body suspension are replaced by a same-line\n\n  Line 2024: rule (a bare argument must start on the same line as its function -- the same rule the\n\n  Line 2031: same-line rule supersedes.\n","metadata":{"matches":13,"truncated":false},"title":"same line|same-line|same_line","time":{"start":1788292261830,"end":1788292261849}},"id":"prt_05e8666a8001aQpozDn6WWesIv","sessionID":"ses_fa17fa8b8ffeRDvLpqU7vbxt5Y","messageID":"msg_05e865aec001yfwgrk5jH9NZ0N"}}
